    "background_story": "Santiago was a charismatic adventurer with a penchant for taking risks. Growing up in a small coastal town, he was always drawn to the sea and the thrill of the unknown. One fateful day, he decided to sail solo across the Atlantic, despite the warnings from seasoned sailors and his worried family. The journey was ill-prepared and inadvisable, but Santiago was undeterred. He faced treacherous storms, equipment failures, and moments of sheer terror, yet he persevered. Miraculously, he made it to the other side, but not without scars, both physical and emotional. Though his feat was impressive, it served as a cautionary tale about the dangers of recklessness. Santiago's story became a legend, a reminder to weigh the risks and consider the consequences before embarking on a perilous journey.",
